CMAA2: https://github.com/GameTechDev/CMAA2
Revision 071c6b0857559f4e36f614362e6d2aab1b61938a, Projects/CMAA2/CMAA2/CMAA2.hlsl.
Copyright 2018 Intel Corporation; author Filip Strugar.
Apache-2.0; see CMAA2-LICENSE and the retained Microsoft helper notice in cmaa2.hlsl.
A dynamic Load offset is added to the coordinates for DXC. GLSL storage formats,
bindings and zero-returning out-of-bounds loads are adapted for Vulkan. Candidate
processing and deferred color application retain the original indirect dispatches.

PSMAA: https://github.com/RdenBlaauwen/PSMAA
Revision 39eb74da55c0663cef22a0f1d4a746ebf33f9e10; bundled dependencies from
the v1.0.0-beta release. Copyright 2025 Robert den Blaauwen. Original code is
MIT; see psmaa/LICENSE and psmaa/reshade-shared/LICENSE. Third-party SMAA,
FidelityFX CAS and BeanSmoothing/TSMAA notices remain in their source headers.
Seven compute passes replace ReShade passes, preserving discarded pixels and
sRGB operations. Depth modulation is disabled. Optional CAS sharpening is not
enabled; the separate host sharpening selector controls RCAS.
The BeanSmoothing/TSMAA permission remains unresolved. LicenseRef-PSMAA-ThirdParty
identifies this uncertainty; it does not grant a new redistribution permission.
This experimental integration is for the requested personal build until the
third-party permission is clarified before publication.

